---Grids subdivide an area into multiple same-size cells which can each contain a child component, with components being
---assigned to cells in the order they're created, from left to right and top to bottom.
---
---Info: Although each cell can only have one component, this can be of any type, even including other grids.
---
---Grid layouts can be configured in one of two modes:
---
---Warning: If the number of child components on a grid exceeds the number of cells, any additional components will
---ignore the grid layout and end up at position 0,0 with a size of 100x100 interface units, indicating a failed layout
---operation.
---@class ui.Grid : ui.ComponentCollection
---@field cellWidth integer (Read-only) The width of each cell in this grid.
---@field cellHeight integer (Read-only) The height of each cell in this grid.
---@field columns integer (Read-only) The number of columns in this grid.
---@field rows integer (Read-only) The number of rows in this grid.
---@field hasFixedCellSizes boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether the cell size for this grid has been explicitly set via `SetCellSize`, resulting in dynamically calculated `columns` and `rows` values based on the grid's dimensions. Otherwise it's `cellWidth` and `cellHeight` that are dynamically calculated.
---@field spacing integer The spacing in interface units between grid cells, both horizontal and vertical.
ui.Grid = {}

---Creates a new Grid on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this grid in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Grid # The newly created grid. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Grid.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Makes the grid use a fixed number of columns and rows, and dynamically scales cell sizes based on that and the grid's
---dimensions.
---
---Warning: Ideally this should only be called on empty grids, as calling this will request layout operations for all
---child components present on the grid.
---@param columns integer The desired number of columns to use for this grid.
---@param rows integer The desired number of rows to use for this grid.
function ui.Grid:SetColumnRows(columns, rows) end

---Makes the grid use fixed cell dimensions, and dynamically scales the number of columns and rows available based on
---that and the grid's dimensions.
---
---Warning: Ideally this should only be called on empty grids, as calling this will request layout operations for all
---child components present on the grid.
---@param width integer The desired width of each cell to use for this grid.
---@param height integer The desired height of each cell to use for this grid.
function ui.Grid:SetCellSize(width, height) end
